    <text>
        <body>
            <div>
                <head>Translated parts</head>
                <p xml:id="CH2e1120-start">
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.1-h" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:26.833+09:00">Book of Music</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:26.833+09:00"/>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:26.833+09:00">Instruments of the Elegant Music Section:</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:26.833+09:00">Their sounds are determined according to the musical pitch standards (lǜ),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:26.833+09:00">each finding its proper place.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:26.833+09:00">When the pitch standard is Huáng Zhōng, then instruments tuned to Huáng Zhōng are used together.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:26.833+09:00">When the pitch standard is Tài Cù, then instruments tuned to Tài Cù are used.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:26.833+09:00">Therefore, the *xuán guān* (旋官, a type of instrument) follows this principle.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:26.833+09:00">If the sounds and pitch standards are completely harmonious,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:26.833+09:00">then there will be no mismatched instruments.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:26.833+09:00">The pitch is universally taken from the middle register to harmonize the musical standards.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:26.833+09:00">Therefore, when Huáng Zhōng is tripled and enlarged to reach the sound of thunder,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.12" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">It is said that the standard of the *huáng zhōng* (黃鍾) pitch pipe is determined by divisions of three.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.13" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">Double an inch</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.14" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">to make one foot and eight inches,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.15" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">then it matches the coarse sound of thunder;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.16" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">subtract nine inches,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.17" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">leaving four inches and five tenths,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.18" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">then it corresponds to the clear sound of the central palace.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.19" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">Only nine inches is considered the correct sound,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.20" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">and can harmonize with spirits and men,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.21" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">and resonate with Heaven and Earth,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.22" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">flowing without ceasing,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.23" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">unifying and transforming.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.24" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">Therefore, the earth's *qì* rises,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.25" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">the sky's *qì* descends,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.26" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">the *yīn* and *yáng* rub against each other,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.27" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">Heaven and Earth stir each other,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.28" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">they are drummed with thunder,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.29" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">roused with wind and rain,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.30" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">moved with the four seasons,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.31" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">and warmed with the sun and moon,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.32" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">and all transformations arise.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.33" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">In this way, music is the harmony of Heaven and Earth.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.34" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">Therefore, the *Shū* (*Shū Jīng* 書經, Classic of Documents) says:</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.35" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">"Pitch relies on prolonged notes,"</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.36" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">"The pitch pipes harmonize the tones,"</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.37" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">then the five tones do not lose their regularity,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.38" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">and the six pitch pipes do not deviate from their standard.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.39" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:16:58.015+09:00">It speaks of the *gū zhú* (孤竹) pipe,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.40" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">The pitch pipes corresponding to the *jiázhōng* pitch</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.41" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">have sounds that harmonize with the *qì*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.42" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">thus they can evoke the celestial spirits to descend.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.43" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">The pipes made of *sūn* bamboo</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.44" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">and corresponding to the *línzhōng* pitch</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.45" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">have sounds that harmonize with the *qì*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.46" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">thus they can evoke the terrestrial deities to emerge.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.47" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">The pipes made of *yīn* bamboo</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.48" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">and corresponding to the *huángzhōng* pitch</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.49" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">have sounds that harmonize with the *qì*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.50" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">thus they can evoke human ghosts to arrive.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-1a.51" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">From the *Taìpíng Yùlǎn*, scroll 565.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00"/>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">Carefully examining:</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">The *Lǐjì Shū* says:</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">"Fúxī's music was called *Lìjī*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">meaning that in the era of Fúxī, the five phases were established.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">The *jiǎzǐ* cycle was the initial foundation.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">He drew the eight trigrams to determine *yīn* and *yáng*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">and created the *qín* and *sè* zithers to harmonize the pitch pipes,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">a music that continued the virtues,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">therefore it was called *Lìjī*.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">Shénnóng's music was called *Xiàmóu*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.12" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">meaning that Shénnóng sowed the hundred grains,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.13" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">benefiting and nurturing all living beings.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.14" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">He created the five-stringed *qín*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.15" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">elaborated on the sixty-four hexagrams,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.16" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:17:21.629+09:00">inherited the foundation and established transformation,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.17" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">In order to establish a plan for inviting the gods,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.18" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">therefore the music is called "Xià Móu" (Descending Plan),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.19" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">in order to demonstrate the accomplishment.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.20" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">The Yellow Emperor's music is called "Yún Mén" (Cloud Gate),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.21" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">saying that the Yellow Emperor's Dao establishes the names of the myriad things,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.22" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">clarifying the people's common wealth,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.23" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">his virtue is like clouds emerging from his gate,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.24" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">the people can possess it within their clans,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.25" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">therefore the music is called "Yún Mén".</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-2a.26" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">"Tàipíng Yùlǎn" (Taiping Imperial Reader), Volume 566.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-3a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00"/>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-3a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">The Chúnyú,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-3a.3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">is made of copper.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-3a.4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">Its copper resembles a bell,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-3a.5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">with a large top and an inverted, contracting mouth,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-3a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">with a crouching beast as a nose on top,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-3a.7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">and a small copper bell tongue suspended inside.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-3a.8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">Whenever music is made,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-3a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">it is shaken to make a sound,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-3a.10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">harmonizing with the drum.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-3a.11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">"Tàipíng Yùlǎn" (Taiping Imperial Reader), Volume 575.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00"/>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">All the instruments made of metal are of six kinds,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">all being types of bells.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">They are called zhōng (bell),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">bó (large bell),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">chún,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">zhuó,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">náo,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">duó (hand bell).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">The bó is like a zhōng but larger.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">Chún,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.12" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">is a Chúnyú,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.13" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:40.499+09:00">round like a mallet;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.14" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">its head,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.15" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">which is large at the top and small at the bottom,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.16" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">is called "metal *chún* and drum."</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.17" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">The *zhuó*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.18" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">is a *zhēng*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.19" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">its shape is like a small bell,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.20" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">used to mark the beat of drums in military marches.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.21" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">The *náo*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.22" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">is like a bell but without a tongue,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.23" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">it has a handle and is held.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.24" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">The *duó* is like a large bell.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-4a.25" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">Same as above.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-5a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00"/>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-5a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">The *zhù*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-5a.3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">its shape is like a *sòng qín*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-5a.4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">it has thirteen strings,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-5a.5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">a thin top,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-5a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">and round shoulders.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-5a.7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">It has frets for tuning,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-5a.8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">the playing method is to hold it with the left hand,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-5a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">and strike it with bamboo in the right hand,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-5a.10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">following the melody and responding to the rhythm.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-5a.11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">From the "Taiping Yulan," volume 576.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00"/>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">The *dí*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">means "to cleanse",</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">made by Qiū Zhòng.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:21:01.45+09:00">It can cleanse away evil influences,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">and broadcast virtuous governance.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">Therefore, Liè Hé (列和) skillfully played it,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">and adjusted the twelve tones to match the musical standards.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">Xún Xù (荀勗) inquired about its essentials,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">and based on three-foot-two measurements, harmonized the pitch,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">cutting the frost-covered bamboo of Yúnmèng (雲夢),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.12" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">imitating the unusual sounds of the dragon's roar.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.13" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">Three holes are for the *yuè* (籥, a type of flute),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.14" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">which is held in civil dances.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.15" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">The people of Bīn (邠) play it.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.16" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">Five holes are for the *zhú* (篴, a type of flute),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.17" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">used in *gāi* music.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.18" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">The music master controls it.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.19" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">Six holes are for the *dí* (笛, flute),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.20" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">which the Qiāng (羌) people play.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.21" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">Seven holes are for the *tiáo* (調, a type of flute),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.22" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">which the Hàn (漢) army uses.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.23" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">The current seven-star flute</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.24" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">is the ancient long flute.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.25" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">A fixed pitch is called *tiáo* (調),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.26" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">which harmonizes with the pitch of bells and chimes,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.27" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:36.235+09:00">each having varying lengths</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.28" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">Yīng lǜ zhī dù.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-6a.29" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">"Tàipíng Yùlǎn" Volume 580.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00"/>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">The *xūn* is *xuān*.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">*Xuān* also means noisy.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">During the time of King Píng of Zhōu 周平王,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">Bào Xīng Gōng 暴辛公 made it by firing clay.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">"Tàipíng Yùlǎn" Volume 581.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">The *léitáo* (thunder drum),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">In the "Zhōu Lǐ" 周禮, "The blind musician (gǔméng) manages the *bōtáo* (rattle drum)."</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">The *táo* is like a drum but smaller,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">with wood piercing it to make a handle.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">The handle has four pieces on each side,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.12" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">creating eight sides.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.13" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">The sides are made of ram skin as ears,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.14" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">shaking it will make it strike itself.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.15" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">The ritual book says:</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.16" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">"The person in charge uses the left hand to shake the *táo*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.17" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">and the right hand to beat the drum," this is it.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-7a.18" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">"Tàipíng Yùlǎn" Volume 82.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-8a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00"/>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-8a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">The sages made the *qiāngjié* (a stringed instrument),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-8a.3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">The *xūn* and *chí* flute arose from this.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-8a.4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">The *zhù* is *zhòng*.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-8a.5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">*Zhòng* also means multitude.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-8a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">It is the sound of the Beginning of Summer,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-8a.7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">when all things take shape in multitude.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-8a.8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:18:58.014+09:00">Each side is two *chǐ* in length,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-8a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00"/>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-8a.10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">Piercing a round hole to the side, a hand inside the hole strikes it,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-8a.11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">in order to raise the sound of the various musical instruments.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-8a.12" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">Same as above.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-9a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00"/>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-9a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">The mùduó 木鐸,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-9a.3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">is a bell.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-9a.4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">It is made of raw bronze</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-9a.5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">and has a tongue made of wood.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-9a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">Therefore, Heaven will use Fūzǐ 夫子 as a mùduó 木鐸,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-9a.7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">meaning when implementing governmental teachings.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-9a.8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">Heaven will command him to issue orders to the world,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-9a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">held and rung during civil dances,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-9a.10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">to promote civil education.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-9a.11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">From the *Tàipíng Yùlǎn* 太平御覽, volume 584.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00"/>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">The jīnduó 金鐸,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">is shaped like the mùduó 木鐸,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">but has a tongue made of metal.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">Its commands serve as a measure,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">ringing out to startle the masses,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">held during military dances,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">to promote military education.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">Same as above.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">The jīn náo 金鐃,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">the smaller ones resemble bells,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.12" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">held and rung,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.13" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:30.576+09:00">to stop the drums.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.14" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:46.768+09:00">Wǔ wǔ,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.15" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:46.768+09:00">the musical instrument held by artisans,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.16" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:46.768+09:00">is said to be shaken and used to dismiss the warriors.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.17" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:46.768+09:00">The large ones</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.18" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:46.768+09:00">are hung up and struck,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.19" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:46.768+09:00">resembling the shape of a bell.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.20" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:46.768+09:00">Around the thin edge, there are twenty-four *xiǎn*,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.21" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:46.768+09:00">corresponding to the musical scales and harmonizing with the music.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#CH2e1120_CHANT_001-10a.22" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-11-10T18:19:46.768+09:00">Same as above.</seg>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
